  "preconditions": [
    "Caller-owned complete XML bytes and seven explicit positive per-document safety limits. Mapping resource/key/hash, source hash and external source context are explicit; no project or write authorization is supplied."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Read and deterministically reserialize typed ReqIF scalar/enumeration definitions and objects; compare lexical values, IDs, metadata, explicit/default/absent provenance and original source bytes/hash.",
    "Project only definition/type IDs and valid JSON-intersection values through the existing bound mapping; independently verify first-export identity hashes and existing-context precedence.",
    "Reject duplicate IDs/attributes, wrong references/types, invalid explicit values and source/mapping conflicts. Preserve nonrepresentable numbers and report object/definition losses without native fallback or default substitution.",
    "Exercise explicit XML limits, DTD/entity/processing-instruction/XInclude rejection, uninterpreted extension retention, resource-error propagation, detached observations and isolated Core/PYZ transport.",
    "Compare declared numeric bounds exactly from lexical decimal values without host integer/exponent or process Decimal-context rounding. Cover date/enum/string/default limits, XML-only lexical whitespace and collisions across deferred ReqIF objects.",
    "Export one existing source object from explicit native fields with source/mapping/context binding; inverse value_map requires one canonical match. Preserve unchanged lexical values, enum order, metadata, absent defaults and other objects; report native remainder and retained nonrepresentable source values.",
    "Reject invalid inverse candidates, changed bindings and ambiguous tables without source mutation. Exercise safe unknown subtrees, malformed XML, configured limits, resource exceptions and isolated distributions."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Der ReqIF-1.2-Import MUSS Spezifikationshierarchien, Objekte, Attribute, Relationen, Datentypen, XHTML-Kerninhalte und referenzierte Anhänge innerhalb des dokumentierten Unterstützungsprofils einlesen können.",
    "scope": "14.h.W passive reqif-object-profile-v1 subset: read/typed preservation/deterministic serialization of supported source definitions and Spec-Objects, explicit bound native mapping projection, source provenance and stable first-export object IDs. No native-field type inference, default materialization, numeric rounding/string fallback or write authority. Unsupported content retains source bytes and blocks a complete serialization claim. All higher ReqIF requirements remain partial. 14.h.R adds exact lexical range validation, the comprehensive boundary/default/safety corpus and a bound inverse mapping for an existing source object. Serialized candidates are revalidated; ambiguous inverse tables conflict, changed native values must reproject exactly, unchanged fields retain source spelling and absence. Metadata and remaining source data are not reconstructed from names. This remains partial ReqIF object transport, not a native project exporter or full integration."
  },
